<http://data.semanticweb.org/ns/swc/ontology#01_introduction> rdfs:label "Introduction" ;
    rdfs:comment "\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tThe Semantic Web Conference ontology (SWC) is an ontology for describing academic conferences. \\n\\t\\t\\t\\tIt was initially designed to support the European Semantic Web Conference,\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tESWC2007, and later extended for both the following conferences in the ESWC series,\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tas well as in the ISWC series.\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tHistorically, the SWC ontology also draws heavily on ontologies developed for\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tESWC2006 and ISWC2006.\\n\\t\\t\\t</p>\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tSWC is mainly a convention of how to use classes and properties from other ontologies, most prominently \\n\\t\\t\\t\\t<a href=\"http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1\">FOAF</a> (for people) and <a href=\"http://ontoware.org/projects/swrc/\">SWRC</a> \\n\\t\\t\\t\\t(their BibTeX elements, for the papers). We are also throwing in some <a href=\"http://sioc-project.org/\">SIOC</a>, \\n\\t\\t\\t\\t<a href=\"http://dublincore.org/documents/dc-rdf/index.shtml\">Dublin Core</a> and \\n\\t\\t\\t\\t<a href=\"http://www.w3.org/TR/rdfcal/\">iCal/RDF Calendar</a>. Our own \\n\\t\\t\\t\\t<a href=\"http://data.semanticweb.org/ns/swc/ontology\">swc namespace</a> provides the glue for all this, as well as \\n\\t\\t\\t\\tspecialised classes for things that have to do with conferences.\\n\\t\\t\\t</p>\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tThis version of SWC has been slimmed down significantly (hence the revision name). A total of 59 classes and 19 properties have been deprecated (deprecated terms can be found at the bottom of this document). This was mostly done with the intention to remove the countless sub-classes of generic classes such as <a href=\"#Chair\">Chair</a> or <a href=\"#SessionEvent\">SessionEvent</a>, which were deemed to be too specific for a general-purpose conference ontology such as SWC. Elsewhere, classes and properties which had never been used and seemed to fall under the heading of \"over-engineering\" were removed. Finally, all CfP related terms were removed. Instead, we suggest to use a dedicated ontology such as the <a href=\"http://sw.deri.org/2005/08/conf/cfp\">CfP ontology</a>.\\n\\t\\t\\t</p>\\n\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t" .

<http://data.semanticweb.org/ns/swc/ontology#02_describing_papers> rdfs:label "Describing Papers" ;
    rdfs:comment "\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>For the basic use case of describing papers, the figure below shows how the main kinds of resources are connected: the paper itself, the authors and their affiliations, and the talk where the paper was presented.\\n\\t\\t\\t</p>\\n\\t\\t\\t<div align=\"center\">\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t<a href=\"documentation/20070921-ISWC+ASWC2007PublicationGraph.pdf\"><img src=\"documentation/20070921-ISWC+ASWC2007PublicationGraph.png\" /></a>\\n\\t\\t\\t</div>\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tThe next figure shows in more detail the kinds of things that can be said about each of the four main entities surrounding a paper.\\n\\t\\t\\t</p>\\n\\t\\t\\t<div align=\"center\">\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t<a href=\"documentation/20071002-Properties.pdf\"><img src=\"documentation/20071002-Properties.png\" /></a>\\n\\t\\t\\t</div>\\n\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t" .

<http://data.semanticweb.org/ns/swc/ontology#03_roles> rdfs:label "Roles" ;
    rdfs:comment "\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tOne of the basic design choices in SWC is to use role modelling for describing the different functions at a conference, such as chairs, reviewers, etc. For any particular role at a given conference, the <code>swc:Role</code> class or a sub-class will be instantiated. This role instance stands in relation to a person (who plays the role) and an event. The figure below gives an example showing how to model the role of the metadata chair (or \"dog food tsar\") at ISWC+ASWC2007, which was held by Knud Möller (together with Tom Heath, not shown in the figure).\\n\\t\\t\\t</p>\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tNote that the metadata chair role is not modelled with its own dedicated class (although it could have been). Instead, an instance of the generic <a href=\"#Chair\">Chair</a> class is used and labelled accordingly.\\n\\t\\t\\t</p>\\n\\t\\t\\t<div align=\"center\">\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t<a href=\"documentation/20090510-Roles_new.pdf\"><img src=\"documentation/20090510-Roles_new.png\" /></a>\\n\\t\\t\\t</div>\\n\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t" .

<http://data.semanticweb.org/ns/swc/ontology#Proceedings> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Proceedings" ;
    dcterms:subject <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Document> ;
    rdfs:comment "\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>The proceedings of a conference or workshop, which contain the papers presented there.</p>\\n\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <http://data.semanticweb.org/ns/swc/ontology#Artefact>,
        foaf:Document ;
    ns1:term_status "testing" .

<http://data.semanticweb.org/ns/swc/ontology#Programme> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Programme" ;
    dcterms:subject <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Document> ;
    rdfs:comment "\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>A document containing the programme of an event such as a conference or workshop. Typically, the programme would list the times and dates for the individual sub-events, e.g., talks, dinners, panel discussions, etc.</p>\\n\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <http://data.semanticweb.org/ns/swc/ontology#Artefact>,
        foaf:Document ;
    ns1:term_status "testing" .

<http://data.semanticweb.org/ns/swc/ontology#attendeeAt> a owl:DeprecatedProperty ;
    rdfs:label "attendee at" ;
    rdfs:comment "\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>Instead of this property, use the <a href=\"#Delegate\">Delegate</a> role.</p>\\n\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t" ;
    rdfs:domain foaf:Person ;
    rdfs:range <http://data.semanticweb.org/ns/swc/ontology#OrganisedEvent> ;
    owl:inverseOf <http://data.semanticweb.org/ns/swc/ontology#hasAttendee> ;
    ns1:term_status "deprecated" .

<http://data.semanticweb.org/ns/swc/ontology#forEvent> a owl:DeprecatedProperty ;
    rdfs:label "for event" ;
    rdfs:comment "\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>The call classes have been deprecated in SWC. Instead, we suggest to use the <a href=\"http://sw.deri.org/2005/08/conf/cfp\">CfP ontology</a>.</p>\\n\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t" ;
    rdfs:domain <http://data.semanticweb.org/ns/swc/ontology#Call> ;
    rdfs:range <http://data.semanticweb.org/ns/swc/ontology#AcademicEvent> ;
    owl:inverseOf <http://data.semanticweb.org/ns/swc/ontology#hasCall> ;
    ns1:term_status "deprecated" .

<http://data.semanticweb.org/ns/swc/ontology#hasAttendee> a owl:DeprecatedProperty ;
    rdfs:label "has attendee" ;
    rdfs:comment "\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>Instead of this property, use the <a href=\"#Delegate\">Delegate</a> role.</p>\\n\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t" ;
    rdfs:domain <http://data.semanticweb.org/ns/swc/ontology#OrganisedEvent> ;
    rdfs:range foaf:Person ;
    owl:inverseOf <http://data.semanticweb.org/ns/swc/ontology#attendeeAt> ;
    ns1:term_status "deprecated" .

<http://data.semanticweb.org/ns/swc/ontology#hasCall> a owl:DeprecatedProperty ;
    rdfs:label "has call" ;
    rdfs:comment "\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>The call classes have been deprecated in SWC. Instead, we suggest to use the <a href=\"http://sw.deri.org/2005/08/conf/cfp\">CfP ontology</a>.</p>\\n\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t" ;
    rdfs:domain <http://data.semanticweb.org/ns/swc/ontology#AcademicEvent> ;
    rdfs:range <http://data.semanticweb.org/ns/swc/ontology#Call> ;
    owl:inverseOf <http://data.semanticweb.org/ns/swc/ontology#forEvent> ;
    ns1:term_status "deprecated" .

<http://data.semanticweb.org/ns/swc/ontology#hasRelatedDocument> a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "has related document" ;
    rdfs:comment "\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tRelates an <a href=\"#AcademicEvent\">event</a> such as a conference, workshop, etc. to a <a href=\"#ArgumentativeDocument\">document</a>.\\n\\t\\t\\t</p>\\n\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t" ;
    rdfs:domain <http://data.semanticweb.org/ns/swc/ontology#AcademicEvent> ;
    rdfs:range <http://data.semanticweb.org/ns/swc/ontology#ArgumentativeDocument> ;
    owl:inverseOf <http://data.semanticweb.org/ns/swc/ontology#relatedToEvent> ;
    ns1:term_status "testing" .

<http://data.semanticweb.org/ns/swc/ontology#hasRole> a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "has role" ;
    rdfs:comment "\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tPart of the <a href=\"#Role\">role</a> modelling machinery of SWC. This property relates an event (e.g. a conference) to a role at the event (e.g. a conference chair).\\n\\t\\t\\t</p>\\n\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t" ;
    rdfs:domain <http://data.semanticweb.org/ns/swc/ontology#AcademicEvent> ;
    rdfs:range <http://data.semanticweb.org/ns/swc/ontology#Role> ;
    owl:inverseOf <http://data.semanticweb.org/ns/swc/ontology#isRoleAt> ;
    ns1:term_status "testing" .

<http://data.semanticweb.org/ns/swc/ontology#heldBy> a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "held by" ;
    rdfs:comment "\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tPart of the <a href=\"#Role\">role</a> modelling machinery of SWC. This property relates a role at an event (e.g. a conference chair) to the person who actually holds the role.\\n\\t\\t\\t</p>\\n\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t" ;
    rdfs:domain <http://data.semanticweb.org/ns/swc/ontology#Role> ;
    rdfs:range foaf:Person ;
    owl:inverseOf <http://data.semanticweb.org/ns/swc/ontology#holdsRole> ;
    ns1:term_status "testing" .

<http://data.semanticweb.org/ns/swc/ontology#holdsRole> a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "holds role" ;
    rdfs:comment "\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tPart of the <a href=\"#Role\">role</a> modelling machinery of SWC. This property relates a person to the role (e.g. a conference chair) it holds at an event.\\n\\t\\t\\t</p>\\n\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t" ;
    rdfs:domain foaf:Person ;
    rdfs:range <http://data.semanticweb.org/ns/swc/ontology#Role> ;
    owl:inverseOf <http://data.semanticweb.org/ns/swc/ontology#heldBy> ;
    ns1:term_status "testing" .

<http://data.semanticweb.org/ns/swc/ontology#isProvidedBy> a owl:DeprecatedProperty ;
    rdfs:label "is provided by" ;
    rdfs:comment "\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>Deprecated because it has never been used and in order to reduce the inflation of ontology terms.</p>\\n\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t" ;
    rdfs:domain <http://data.semanticweb.org/ns/swc/ontology#Sponsorship> ;
    rdfs:range foaf:Organisation ;
    owl:inverseOf <http://data.semanticweb.org/ns/swc/ontology#isProviderOf> ;
    ns1:term_status "deprecated" .

<http://data.semanticweb.org/ns/swc/ontology#isProviderOf> a owl:DeprecatedProperty ;
    rdfs:label "is provider of" ;
    rdfs:comment "\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>Deprecated because it has never been used and in order to reduce the inflation of ontology terms.</p>\\n\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t" ;
    rdfs:domain foaf:Organisation ;
    rdfs:range <http://data.semanticweb.org/ns/swc/ontology#Sponsorship> ;
    owl:inverseOf <http://data.semanticweb.org/ns/swc/ontology#isProvidedBy> ;
    ns1:term_status "deprecated" .

<http://data.semanticweb.org/ns/swc/ontology#isRoleAt> a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "is role at" ;
    rdfs:comment "\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tPart of the <a href=\"#Role\">role</a> modelling machinery of SWC. This property relates a role at an event (e.g. a conference chair) to the event (e.g. a conference).\\n\\t\\t\\t</p>\\n\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t" ;
    rdfs:domain <http://data.semanticweb.org/ns/swc/ontology#Role> ;
    rdfs:range <http://data.semanticweb.org/ns/swc/ontology#AcademicEvent> ;
    owl:inverseOf <http://data.semanticweb.org/ns/swc/ontology#hasRole> ;
    ns1:term_status "testing" .

<http://data.semanticweb.org/ns/swc/ontology#isSubEventOf> a owl:TransitiveProperty ;
    rdfs:label "is a sub-event of",
        "is sub-event of" ;
    rdfs:comment "Events can be sub-events of other events. E.g., a talk can be a sub-event of a session, which in turn can be a sub-event of a conference. The relation is transitive - the talk is also a sub-event of the conference." ;
    rdfs:domain <http://www.w3.org/2002/12/cal/ical#Vevent> ;
    rdfs:range <http://www.w3.org/2002/12/cal/ical#Vevent> ;
    owl:inverseOf <http://data.semanticweb.org/ns/swc/ontology#isSuperEventOf> ;
    ns1:term_status "testing" .

<http://data.semanticweb.org/ns/swc/ontology#isSuperEventOf> a owl:TransitiveProperty ;
    rdfs:label "is super-event of",
        "is the super-event of" ;
    rdfs:comment "Events can be super-events of other events. E.g., a conference can be the super-event of a session, which in turn can be the super-event of a talk. The relation is transitive - the conference is also the super-event of the talk." ;
    rdfs:domain <http://www.w3.org/2002/12/cal/ical#Vevent> ;
    rdfs:range <http://www.w3.org/2002/12/cal/ical#Vevent> ;
    owl:inverseOf <http://data.semanticweb.org/ns/swc/ontology#isSubEventOf> ;
    ns1:term_status "testing" .

<http://data.semanticweb.org/ns/swc/ontology#license_doc> rdfs:label "License Statement" ;
    rdfs:comment "\\n\\t\\t\\t<!-- Creative Commons License -->\\n\\t\\t\\t<p class=\"copyright\">\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tCopyright &copy; 2007-2009 Knud Möller, Sean Bechhofer and Tom Heath.<br/>\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t<br/>\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t<a href=\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/\"><img alt=\"Creative Commons License\" style=\"border: 0; float: right; padding: 10px;\" src=\"somerights.gif\" /></a>\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tThis work is licensed under a <a href=\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/\">Creative Commons Attribution License</a>. \\n\\t\\t\\t\\tThis copyright applies to the <em>Semantic Web Conference Ontology (SWC) Specification</em> and accompanying documentation in RDF.\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tRegarding underlying technology, SWC uses W3C's <a href=\"http://www.w3.org/RDF/\">RDF</a> technology, an\\n\\t\\t\\t\\topen Web standard that can be freely used by anyone.\\n\\t\\t\\t</p>\\n\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t" .

<http://data.semanticweb.org/ns/swc/ontology#relatedToEvent> a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "related to Event",
        "related to event" ;
    rdfs:comment "\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tRelates a <a href=\"#ArgumentativeDocument\">document</a> to an <a href=\"#AcademicEvent\">event</a> such as a conference, workshop, etc.\\n\\t\\t\\t</p>\\n\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t" ;
    rdfs:domain <http://data.semanticweb.org/ns/swc/ontology#ArgumentativeDocument>,
        <http://data.semanticweb.org/ns/swc/ontology#Artefact> ;
    rdfs:range <http://data.semanticweb.org/ns/swc/ontology#AcademicEvent> ;
    owl:inverseOf <http://data.semanticweb.org/ns/swc/ontology#hasRelatedDocument> ;
    ns1:term_status "testing" .

<http://data.semanticweb.org/ns/swc/swrc> a owl:Ontology .

<http://data.semanticweb.org/ns/swc/swrc-topics> a owl:Ontology .

<http://swrc.ontoware.org/ontology#InProceedings> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <http://data.semanticweb.org/ns/swc/ontology#Paper> .

foaf:Group a owl:Class .

foaf:member a owl:ObjectProperty .

<http://xmlns.com/wordnet/1.6/Announcement> a owl:Class .

<http://xmlns.com/wordnet/1.6/Document> a owl:Class .

<http://xmlns.com/wordnet/1.6/Event-1> a owl:Class .

<http://xmlns.com/wordnet/1.6/Menu> a owl:Class .

<http://xmlns.com/wordnet/1.6/Role-1> a owl:Class .

<http://xmlns.com/wordnet/1.6/Sponsorship> a owl:Class .

<http://data.semanticweb.org/ns/swc/ontology#MealEvent> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Meal Event" ;
    dcterms:subject <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Event> ;
    rdfs:comment "\\n\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tA lunch, dinner or similar event at a conference or conference-like event.\\n\\t\\t\\t</p>\\n\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <http://data.semanticweb.org/ns/swc/ontology#NonAcademicEvent> ;
    ns1:term_status "testing" .

<http://data.semanticweb.org/ns/swc/ontology#Place> a owl:DeprecatedClass ;
    rdfs:label "Place" ;
    dcterms:subject <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Place> ;
    rdfs:comment "\\n\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tDeprecated: no real need to have an internal super-class for locations, we can just use the <a href=\"&geo;SpatialThing\">SpatialThing</a>.\\n\\t\\t\\t</p>\\n\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.w3.org/2003/01/geo/wgs84_pos#SpatialThing> ;
    ns1:term_status "deprecated" .

<http://data.semanticweb.org/ns/swc/ontology#TrackEvent> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Track Event" ;
    dcterms:subject <http://data.semanticweb.org/ns/swc/ontology#AcademicEvent> ;
    rdfs:comment "\\n\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tA track groups all those sessions or events at a conference or workshop that belong to a common, overall theme. Depending on the conference, tracks can be quite generic, such as \"Research\" or \"Industrial\", but can also be more specific, such as \"Semantic Web\" or \"Numismatics\". SWC does not define any specific tracks, since conferences often differ so much with respect to how they structure their tracks, that it would be pointless to try and find a set of tracks that would suit all conferences.\\n\\t\\t\\t</p>\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>Sub-classes of TrackEvent which were defined in previous versions of the SWC ontology are now deprecated.</p>\\n\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <http://data.semanticweb.org/ns/swc/ontology#AcademicEvent> ;
    ns1:term_status "testing" .

<http://swrc.ontoware.org/ontology#ResearchTopic> a owl:Class .

<http://data.semanticweb.org/ns/swc/ontology#BreakEvent> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Break Event" ;
    dcterms:subject <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Event> ;
    rdfs:comment "\\n\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tAny kind of break at the super-event, such as a coffee break.\\n\\t\\t\\t</p>\\n\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <http://data.semanticweb.org/ns/swc/ontology#NonAcademicEvent> ;
    ns1:term_status "testing" .

<http://data.semanticweb.org/ns/swc/ontology#Paper> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Paper" ;
    dcterms:subject <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Document> ;
    rdfs:comment "\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>A scientific/scholarly paper, e.g., an article in a scientific journal, or a paper at a conference or workshop. A paper could also be unpublished formally, as long as it has the form of a scientific paper (introduction, conclusion, related work, etc.).</p>\\n\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <http://data.semanticweb.org/ns/swc/ontology#ArgumentativeDocument>,
        <http://data.semanticweb.org/ns/swc/ontology#Artefact> ;
    ns1:term_status "testing" .

<http://data.semanticweb.org/ns/swc/ontology#SessionEvent> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Session Event" ;
    dcterms:subject <http://data.semanticweb.org/ns/swc/ontology#AcademicEvent> ;
    rdfs:comment "\\n\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tA session dedicated to a specific topic at a conference. This could be a session with talks, or also a poster session, a demo session, or any other kind of session.\\n\\t\\t\\t</p>\\n\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <http://data.semanticweb.org/ns/swc/ontology#AcademicEvent> ;
    ns1:term_status "testing" .

<http://data.semanticweb.org/ns/swc/ontology#SocialEvent> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Social Event" ;
    dcterms:subject <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Event> ;
    rdfs:comment "\\n\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tExamples for social events are parties or excursions.\\n\\t\\t\\t</p>\\n\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <http://data.semanticweb.org/ns/swc/ontology#NonAcademicEvent> ;
    ns1:term_status "testing" .

foaf:Document a owl:Class .

foaf:Organization a owl:Class .

<http://data.semanticweb.org/person/sean-bechhofer> a foaf:Person ;
    foaf:homepage <http://www.cs.man.ac.uk/~seanb/> ;
    foaf:name "Sean Bechhofer" ;
    foaf:surname "Bechhofer" .

<http://kantenwerk.org/metadata/foaf.rdf#me> a foaf:Person ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <http://kantenwerk.org/metadata/foaf.rdf> ;
    foaf:homepage <http://kantenwerk.org> ;
    foaf:name "Knud Möller" ;
    foaf:surname "Möller" .

<http://tomheath.com/id/me> a foaf:Person ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <http://tomheath.com/home/rdf> ;
    foaf:homepage <http://tomheath.com/home/html> ;
    foaf:name "Tom Heath" ;
    foaf:surname "Heath" .

<http://data.semanticweb.org/ns/swc/ontology#ArgumentativeDocument> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Argumentative Document" ;
    dcterms:subject <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Document> ;
    rdfs:comment "\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>An argumentative document is a document which uses analytical reasoning and evidence in order to argue for a point of view. Typical examples are scientific papers or political pamphlets. Negative examples are novels or plays (even though a novel might also try to sway the reader to a certain point of view).</p>\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>According to <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Text_types\">Text Types</a>, an argumentative document is based \"on the evaluation and the subsequent subjective judgement in answer to a problem. It refers to the reasons advanced for or against a matter\".</p>\\n\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Text_types> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf foaf:Document ;
    ns1:term_status "testing" .

<http://data.semanticweb.org/ns/swc/ontology#NonAcademicEvent> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Non-academic Event" ;
    dcterms:subject <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Event> ;
    rdfs:comment "\\n\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tIn the context of SWC, a non-academic event is any kind or <a href=\"#OrganisedEvent\">organised event</a> which does not concern the topic or theme of the conference as such. Examples are breaks, dinners, parties, etc.\\n\\t\\t\\t</p>\\n\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <http://data.semanticweb.org/ns/swc/ontology#OrganisedEvent> ;
    ns1:term_status "testing" .

<http://data.semanticweb.org/ns/swc/ontology#Sponsorship> a owl:DeprecatedClass ;
    rdfs:label "Sponsorship" ;
    rdfs:comment "\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>Deprecated because it has never been used and in order to reduce the inflation of ontology terms.</p>\\n\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <http://xmlns.com/wordnet/1.6/Sponsorship> ;
    ns1:term_status "deprecated" .

<http://www.w3.org/2002/12/cal/ical#Vevent> a owl:Class .

<http://data.semanticweb.org/ns/swc/ontology#TalkEvent> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Talk Event" ;
    dcterms:subject <http://data.semanticweb.org/ns/swc/ontology#AcademicEvent> ;
    rdfs:comment "\\n\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tA speaker giving a talk. This could be the presentation of a paper, but also keynote speech or any other kind of talk.\\n\\t\\t\\t</p>\\n\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <http://data.semanticweb.org/ns/swc/ontology#AcademicEvent> ;
    ns1:term_status "testing" .

<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Call> rdfs:label "Call" .

<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Place> rdfs:label "Place" .

<http://www.w3.org/2003/01/geo/wgs84_pos#SpatialThing> a owl:Class .

<http://data.semanticweb.org/ns/swc/ontology#Artefact> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Artefact" ;
    dcterms:subject <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Document> ;
    rdfs:comment "\\n\\t\\t\\t<p><emph>Artefact</emph> here means a document which can have a physical manifestation, like a paper or the proceedings of a conference.</p>\\n\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <http://xmlns.com/wordnet/1.6/Document> ;
    ns1:term_status "testing" .

<http://data.semanticweb.org/ns/swc/ontology#OrganisedEvent> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Organised Event" ;
    dcterms:subject <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Event> ;
    rdfs:comment "\\n\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>An event in time and space which is planned and organised, as opposed to something which 'just happens', such as a car accident or sunset.</p>\\n\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.w3.org/2002/12/cal/ical#Vevent>,
        <http://xmlns.com/wordnet/1.6/Event-1> ;
    ns1:term_status "testing" .

foaf:Person a owl:Class .

<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Document> rdfs:label "Document" .

<http://data.semanticweb.org/ns/swc/ontology#Call> a owl:DeprecatedClass ;
    rdfs:label "Call" ;
    dcterms:subject <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Call> ;
    rdfs:comment "\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>The call classes have been deprecated in SWC. Instead, we suggest to use the <a href=\"http://sw.deri.org/2005/08/conf/cfp\">CfP ontology</a>.</p>\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>A <emph>call</emph> is a public announcement, asking for contribution of some kind to events such as conferences or workshops, or to a publication such as a journal or book.</p>\\n\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <http://xmlns.com/wordnet/1.6/Announcement> ;
    ns1:term_status "deprecated" .

<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Event> rdfs:label "Event, other" .

<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Role> rdfs:label "Role" .

<http://data.semanticweb.org/ns/swc/ontology#AcademicEvent> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Academic Event" ;
    dcterms:subject <http://data.semanticweb.org/ns/swc/ontology#AcademicEvent> ;
    rdfs:comment "\\n\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>Academic events are e.g. conferences and conference-like events, and all the sub-events of those which are about the topic or theme of the conference, such as talks or panels.</p>\\n\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <http://data.semanticweb.org/ns/swc/ontology#OrganisedEvent> ;
    ns1:term_status "testing" .

<http://data.semanticweb.org/ns/swc/ontology#Role> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Role" ;
    dcterms:subject <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Role> ;
    rdfs:comment "\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tRole is the super-class of all the different roles performed at a conference or workshop. Examples are the various conference chairs, the delegates, presenters, PC members, etc. The intended use of this class is that an instance of Role will be related to the event at which it is performed, and to the person which performs it.\\n\\t\\t\\t</p>\\n\\t\\t\\t<p>\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tSince the set of roles is slightly different for each event, and since it would therefore be impossible to provide sub-classes for all needs and circumstances, the SWC ontology only contains a very basic set of Role classes. Rather than diversifying the set of Role classes to cater for all needs, users should instead instantiate the small set of different Role classes and cover the roles at a specific event in this way. E.g., instead of sub-classing the Chair role with MainChair, WorkshopChair, TutorialChair, etc., the different kinds of chairs should simply be instances of the generic Chair class and be labelled appropriately.\\n\\t\\t\\t</p>\\n\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <http://xmlns.com/wordnet/1.6/Role-1> ;
    ns1:term_status "testing" .

